Adapted material (see each file's header for its changes; the Apache
License 2.0 text is in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt):

  - crates/pitwall-detect/detect/claude.toml and codex.toml are derived from
    Herdr's agent detection manifests (src/detect/manifests/claude.toml and
    codex.toml). Modified: schema simplified for Pitwall's rule engine,
    regions narrowed, rules added and removed.
  - crates/pitwall-detect/detect/gemini.toml, opencode.toml, cursor.toml,
    copilot.toml, qwen.toml and amp.toml are derived from Herdr's manifests
    of the same agents (src/detect/manifests/gemini.toml, opencode.toml,
    cursor.toml, github-copilot.toml, qwen.toml and amp.toml). Modified:
    schema simplified, whole-screen regions narrowed to the bottom of the
    screen, the OSC progress rule dropped, detail hints and an explicit idle
    fallback (Herdr's engine default for known agents) added.
  - crates/pitwall-detect/src/detect/tests_more_agents.rs uses screens built
    from the UI strings in those Herdr manifests.
  - The rule model in crates/pitwall-detect/src/detect.rs (priority-ordered
    rules over screen regions with contains/regex/line_regex and all/any/not
    gates, and the region helpers such as the prompt box and the Codex
    prompt marker) follows the design of Herdr's src/detect/manifest.rs.
  - The launch and resume fields in crates/pitwall-core/agents/gemini.toml,
    opencode.toml, copilot.toml and qwen.toml follow Herdr's agent
    integrations (src/agent_resume.rs).

  crates/pitwall-detect/detect/aider.toml is not derived from Herdr (Herdr
  has no Aider manifest); it was written for Pitwall.

